 ### Automatic updates and the vulnerability gate
 
-Each container has two settings (`action.updates`, table
+Each container has three settings (`action.updates`, table
 `docker_container_settings`):
 
 - **Update automatically** - the container is picked by the scheduled
   task *Update Docker containers* with the scope "Those set to update
   automatically". Nothing updates on its own without such a task.
+- **How far automatic updates may go** (`update_policy`,
+  [`app/services/update_policy.py`](https://github.com/sparkycz1/debcontrol/blob/main/app/services/update_policy.py)) -
+  *Any newer image* (`any`, the default and what every container did
+  before 0.125.0), *Minor and patch versions* (`minor`: never a new major
+  version) or *Patch versions only* (`patch`: same major.minor). It
+  applies to that scheduled scope only; an update started by hand (or by
+  the scopes "with a newer image" / "all") is not limited. Two parts:
+  - **The guard**, for every container: after the pull, the version the
+    new image declares (`org.opencontainers.image.version`) is compared
+    with the running image's (or, when that declares none, with its
+    version tag). Outside the policy - or when the new image declares no
+    version - nothing changes: the tag points at the running image again
+    and the job ends **skipped** with the versions in its message.
+  - **The tag bump**, for a container not created by Compose on a version
+    tag (`nginx:1.27.3`): the newest tag of the same shape (same `v`,
+    flavour like `-alpine`, number of parts) the policy allows is pulled
+    from its public registry (the ones listed on
+    [Monitoring](Monitoring#docker-containers)) and the container is
+    recreated on it (`nginx:1.27.4` for `patch`, `1.29.0` for `minor`).
+    *Roll back* after such an update goes back to the old tag too. A
+    Compose container keeps its tag - its compose file decides - and the
+    containers table shows the newer tag the policy allows as a hint
+    ("change the tag in the compose file"); for any other container it
+    shows where the next automatic update moves.
 - **Vulnerability gate** - what stops its updates
   ([`app/services/docker_gate.py`](https://github.com/sparkycz1/debcontrol/blob/main/app/services/docker_gate.py)):
 
@@ -240,6 +269,32 @@ machine (`Machine.docker_vulnerabilities`) and feed the notification
